of my life; and for what cause it seems mysterious, unless I was ordained from before the foundation of the world for some good end, or bad, as you may choose to call it. Judge ye for yourselves. God knoweth all these things, whether it be good or bad. But nevertheless, deep water is what I am wont to swim in. It all has become a second nature to me; and I feel, like Paul, to glory in tribulation; for to this day has the God of my fathers delivered me out of them all, and will deliver me from henceforth; for behold, and lo, I shall triumph over all my enemies, for the Lord God hath spoken it.","n":2,"sm":"Ma o tugā ua valaaulia a’u ou te ala atu ai, e peiseai ua nao se mea faatauvaa ia mea ia te a’u, ona o le lotovale ma le ita o tagata ua avea ma o’u tulaga masani i aso uma o lo’u olaga; ma o le a se pogai e foliga mai ai o se mealilo lea, vagana ai na faauuina a’u a o le’i faavaeina le lalolagi mo se faamoemoe lelei, pe leaga, e pei ona outou filifili e ta’u ai. Ia outou faamasino mo outou lava. Ua silafia e le Atua ia mea uma, pe lelei pe leaga. Ae e ui i lea, o le vai loloto o le mea lea ua masani ona ou aau ai. Ua avea ia mea uma ma uiga masani ia te a’u; ma ua ou lagona, e pei o Paulo, e olioli i puapuaga; ona ua laveaiina a’u i fafo e le Atua o o’u tamā mai nei puapuaga uma e oo mai i le aso nei, ma o le a ia laveaiina a’u mai le taimi nei ma le agai i luma; aua faauta, ma taga’i, o le a ou manumalo i o’u fili uma, aua ua fetalai mai ai le Alii le Atua.","w":[{"en":"and","sm":"Ma"},{"en":"of","sm":"o"},{"en":"","sm":"tugā"},{"en":"·","sm":"ua"},{"en":"·","sm":"valaaulia"},{"en":"I am called","sm":"a’u"},{"en":"·","sm":"ou"},{"en":"I","sm":"te"},{"en":"through","sm":"ala"},{"en":"","sm":"atu"},{"en":"","sm":"ai,"},{"en":"·","sm":"e"},{"en":"as it were","sm":"peiseai"},{"en":"","sm":"ua"},{"en":"","sm":"nao"},{"en":"·","sm":"se"},{"en":"a thing","sm":"mea"},{"en":"the simpleness","sm":"faatauvaa"},{"en":"·","sm":"ia"},{"en":"these things","sm":"mea"},{"en":"·",